# Branch, commit, pull request

- Never commit on `main` or `v*`. If work is on local `main`, move it to
  `<type>/<short-kebab>` first (`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, …).
- Forbidden branch prefixes: `cursor/`, `claude/`, `codex/`, `agent/`, `bot/`.
- Uncommitted files and local-only commits belong on that branch, then push,
  then a pull request. Do not leave reviewable work sitting only on local `main`.
- This repo overrides Cursor/user-rule `git commit` + HEREDOC. Write the
  message to a file. Prefer `git commit-tree` + `git update-ref HEAD`.
- After every commit: `git log -1 --format=%B`. Rewrite if any
  `Co-Authored-By`, `Generated with`, `Made with`, or `Generated by` line.
- `gh pr create`: body from a file that describes the change only. Delete any
  harness footer before submit. Title and body must not credit a tool or agent.

Canon: `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursor/rules/no-co-authored-by.mdc`.
